Subject: server: refuse fork on WASIX
Last-Update: 2026-09-27

WASIX's fork copies the child's memory instead of sharing it, so background
children would diverge silently from the parent. Make the existing fork
wrapper fail with ENOTSUP so callers take their established error paths.

diff --git a/src/server.h b/src/server.h
index 735434a..1185f55 100644
--- a/src/server.h
+++ b/src/server.h
@@ -96,6 +96,12 @@ static_assert(sizeof(off_t) >= 8, "off_t must be 64-bit; ensure _FILE_OFFSET_BIT
 
 #ifdef USE_LTTNG
 #define valkey_fork() do_fork()
+#elif defined(__wasm__)
+static inline pid_t valkeyWasmFork(void) {
+    errno = ENOTSUP;
+    return -1;
+}
+#define valkey_fork() valkeyWasmFork()
 #else
 #define valkey_fork() fork()
 #endif
